{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Heads of the tribes</b> — 'Heads of the tribes' is juxtaposed to vows and freewill offerings, as it is written above: 'apart from your vows and your freewill offerings.' This teaches that the heads of the tribes coerce the bringing of vows and freewill offerings, as we say: a warning to the court to enforce them. Likewise the festivals are fixed by the mouths of the heads of the tribes. And furthermore, when Israel is in distress, their heads make vows, as with Jephthah. Likewise the chiefs of the thousands, 'and he brought the offering of YHWH.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:23.433275546Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}